# Read a whole knowledge base on one board > Why not merge everything
# ipm-overview:docs/use-cases/read-a-board.md#L146
# ef1b92d59b7512ac69f84f6910bebca21635b2ee

# The union is its own run of the same tool, so its own whole event: the
# board run collects fragments and keeps them; this one reads and merges.
whole::a Build a union graph of a corpus ::e

read::a Read the corpus into fragments ::e
  --> merge::a Merge same-named nodes ::e
read, merge --::P--> whole

union::a ipm-graph-union --> read, merge
corpus::a the pages of a knowledge base --> read
graph::a corpus.ipm.json --> merge

union --> union builder ::c, command-line tool ::c
corpus --> ipm knowledge base ::c
graph --> union graph ::c, output ::c
